  "term": "fibril",
  "definition": "In this context, a fibril is a preformed thread-like aggregate of alpha-synuclein that can spread and contribute to toxic protein buildup seen in Parkinson’s disease models. It refers to a biologically aggregated form of a protein rather than its normal state.",
